# Demo capture "gp" (tools/video/capture.sh gp): the same start as demo-boot (Start, the controls
# panel hidden, the opening), then title -> licence 1 -> Single Player -> Grand Prix -> 50cc ->
# Mario, Standard Kart M, automatic drift -> Mushroom Cup -> Start Race: OK, with the driving bot
# started (kart-bot.js): the first race (Luigi Circuit, 12 karts, items) driven by the bot through a
# fake gamepad, with the player's own camera and HUD. Marks: page, start, title, main-menu, ok (the
# press that loads the race); the capture's perf.json adds race-loaded from the game's own log.
#
# Needs a licence in slot 1: the site's game folder seeds a save (tools/hosting/stage-game.sh
# --save rksys.dat; one exported from any run with the page's Export save button will do).
#
# Left click is A, and every press counts (see demo-timetrial.cmds): the route anchors on the
# game's title-scene line and leaves each menu time to slide in.
mark page
waitstart 90000
mark start
wait 2500
eval document.getElementById('hide-controls').click()
waitlog 120 RVL_SDK - THP
mark title
wait 3000
# title -> Select License (licence 1 under the cursor) -> main menu
click 500 430
wait 3000
click 500 430
wait 4500
mark main-menu
# Single Player -> Grand Prix (under the cursor) -> Engine Classes (50cc under the cursor)
click 500 430
wait 8000
click 500 430
wait 4500
shot engine-class
# 50cc -> Mario -> Standard Kart M -> automatic -> Mushroom Cup -> Start Race screen
click 500 430
wait 4500
click 500 430
wait 4500
click 500 430
wait 4500
click 500 430
wait 4500
click 500 430
wait 4500
shot start-race
eval window.__mkwBot.start()
mark ok
click 500 430
waitlog 30 \[bot\] route
# the race: the course flyover and countdown (about 20 s), then the first two laps or so
wait 30000
wait 30000
wait 20000
mark end
wait 500
